<%# locals: (item:) %>

<%#
  The row's comment and receipt counts, wrapped so a stream can swap in fresh
  ones, even when a badge is hidden at zero. `contents` keeps the badges direct
  flex items of the memo cell.

  Replaced with `turbo_stream.replace [item, :badges]` by:
  - ReceiptsController, when one of the item's receipts changes
  - CommentsController#destroy, when one of the item's comments is deleted
  - the transaction popovers, which reload after a comment is posted

  The counts are cached on the item (see Ledger::Item#refresh!), and each of
  those changes refreshes them before the stream renders. The exception is
  comments shared with the other side of a transfer, which don't refresh the
  item's count yet.
%>
<div id="<%= dom_id(item, :badges) %>" class="contents">
  <%= list_badge_for auditor_signed_in? ? item.comment_count : item.not_admin_only_comment_count, "comment", "post", optional: true %>
  <%= list_badge_for item.receipt_count, "receipt", "payment-docs", optional: item.receipt_optional?, required: item.missing_receipt? %>
</div>
